      "description": "Watch LDU de Quito vs Palmeiras highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 17, 2026. The CONMEBOL Libertadores delivered a classic encounter on 2026-09-17 , as the high altitude of Quito played host to a dramatic clash between LDU de Quito and Palmeiras . What started as a tactical battle evolved into a chaotic masterpiece, ultimately requiring a penalty shootout to separate two continental giants. Early Trading of Blows The match ignited early when Marlon Freitas found the back of the net for Palmeiras in the 10th minute, silencing the local crowd. However, the lead was short-lived. Just five minutes later, LDU de Quito struck back through Luis Segovia , who capitalized on an assist from Lucas Rodriguez to restore parity. The first half continued at a relentless pace, with the referee issuing yellow cards to Jose Lopez and Juan Rodriguez as both sides fought for dominance. Estrada Sparks a Stoppage-Time Miracle The narrative took a sharp turn in the 73rd minute when Vitor Roque stepped up to convert a penalty, putting Palmeiras ahead 2-1. As the clock hit the 90-minute mark, the Brazilians looked poised to escape with a victory. But Michael Estrada had other plans. In a stunning display of predatory finishing, Estrada leveled the score at 2-2 in the 90th minute before heading home a dramatic winner in the 93rd minute following a cross from Alexander Alvarado . The Final Verdict from the Spot With the match ending 3-2 in favor of LDU de Quito on the night and the aggregate score leveled, the tie proceeded to a penalty shootout. The tension was suffocating. Luis Segovia and Lucas Rodriguez missed their attempts for the hosts, while Palmeiras remained resilient. Despite misses from Lucas Evangelista and Vitor Roque , successful penalties from Felipe Anderson , Joaquin Piquerez , Mauricio , and Deyverson ensured that the Brazilian side would progress after a night of pure footballing madness."
